^["open"]{
 ?[prose_chunks]: "which #-lines in the corpus still lex as ProseChunk after PARTICLE lexing (plain # comments only, or bare #>/#: without a name too) — decides whether the ~[lattice_registry] glossary needs a prose-fallback rule?"
 ?[pattern_refactors]: "census names the recurring header particle stacks; which of them (if any) earn a mechanical refactor at ~[lattice_registry] is a per-pattern call for the user."
 ?[header_stack_value]: "Across 70 wip.spw headers, #:layer #!pragmatics is in all 70, #:plan #!<lane> restates the card glyph in all 70, and no #>plan_<slug> anchor is cited outside its own file; retire the stack from the wip template, or give each particle something only it says?"
 ?[value_unit]: "What is a particle worth: the bits it carries in its slot, the bits left once the glyph, path and slug are known, the citations it receives, the tools that read it, or the creator's felt verdict; and which of them does hover show first?"
 ?[stance_name]: "The ~# stance is not an aim: ~#key: value is a field (15909 uses, cache and intent fields) and ~#name(…) an apposition, ~#lens(…) now read as the lens reading; is field the name for the first, and does the stance itself (~ on the # plane, beside plain #) need a name of its own?"
}

